  "heroLede": "Five countries. One question. One right order. A daily geography game built entirely on real figures — each one showing you exactly where it came from.",
  "@heroLede": {
    "description": "Under the heading."
  },
  "exampleQuestion": "Which of these has the longest coastline?",
  "@exampleQuestion": {
    "description": "A sample question; the five country names below come from CLDR."
  },
  "exampleText": "You drag them into order and find out at once — not just whether you were right, but by how much, and which pairs you had the wrong way round. Then the harder version of the same fact: which has the most coastline <em>for its size</em>? Canada no longer wins. The Maldives does.",
  "@exampleText": {
    "description": "Keep the <em>…</em> around 'for its size'."
  },
  "card1Title": "A puzzle a day",
  "@card1Title": {
    "description": "Card heading."
  },
  "card1Text": "One daily puzzle everyone in the world gets, the same for you and everyone else, playable offline. Plus endless play whenever you want more.",
  "@card1Text": {
    "description": "Card text."
  },
  "card2Title": "Real numbers, shown honestly",
  "@card2Title": {
    "description": "Card heading."
  },
  "card2Text": "Every figure names its source, its publication and its year. Your score is one number, and you can always see the arithmetic behind it.",
  "@card2Text": {
    "description": "Card text."
  },
  "card3Title": "It teaches while you play",
  "@card3Title": {
    "description": "Card heading."
  },
  "card3Text": "Getting it wrong tells you something true: which country actually has more, and by how much. That is the whole point.",
  "@card3Text": {
    "description": "Card text."
  },
  "card4Title": "The world opens up",
  "@card4Title": {
    "description": "Card heading."
  },
  "card4Text": "You start with countries most people know and earn your way outward, unlocking new places and new questions as you play.",
  "@card4Text": {
    "description": "Card text."
  },
  "whyTitle": "Why sorting?",
  "@whyTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading."
  },
  "whyText": "\"What is the area of Kazakhstan?\" is a fact to memorise. \"Is Kazakhstan bigger than Argentina?\" is a judgement you can actually make — and get better at. Relative judgement is a skill people enjoy exercising, and one that improves with practice. That is what the game trains.",
  "@whyText": {
    "description": "Section text."
  },
  "honestyTitle": "Honesty, specifically",
  "@honestyTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading."
  },
  "honestyText": "Puzzle games can be loose with numbers. This one is not. Every value is traced to a single named publication with a date, and if a source has nothing to say about a country then that country is left out of the question rather than given a zero or a guess. Where the licence for a figure does not permit us to use it, the question does not ship — even when losing it hurts. The full list of sources is <a href=\"credits.html\">published here</a>, generated from the data the app itself carries.",
  "@honestyText": {
    "description": "Keep the <a href=\"credits.html\">…</a> link around 'published here'."
  },
  "notifyLabel": "Leave an address and we will tell you when it ships.",
  "@notifyLabel": {
    "description": "Signup form label."
  },
  "notifyButton": "Tell me at launch",
  "@notifyButton": {
    "description": "Signup button."
  },
  "notifyFine": "A note straight away to confirm, then a message when the game ships and when new ways to sort arrive. Nothing else, and no trackers on this site. Every message carries an unsubscribe link, and using it deletes the address.",
  "@notifyFine": {
    "description": "Small print under the form."
  },
